# Normalize line endings to LF in the repository.
#
# The target runtime is Linux (Replit runs `sh -c "npm ci && npm run build"`),
# and several files here are executed rather than only read: the .mjs build and
# verification scripts. Storing CRLF for those is how you get an intermittent
# "Unexpected token" or a shebang that the shell will not honour. Normalizing
# once here is cheaper than debugging it later on someone else's machine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be touched by the above.
*.woff2 binary
*.woff binary
*.ttf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary

# A patch-style file: CRLF in a diff is noise.
*.patch -text